Q: In a C++ class, how do I declare friendship with a templated function in another namespace? A: <p>One way is to forward declare the <code>ns::foo</code> function template before <code>A</code>:</p>
<pre class="lang-cpp prettyprint-override"><code>namespace ns {
template &lt;class T&gt;
T foo(int);
}

class A {
    template &lt;class T&gt;
    friend T ns::foo(int); // and qualify it with ns here

   private:
    int x;
};
</code></pre>
<p>Then accessing the private members will be ok in all <code>ns::foo(int)</code>s:</p>
<pre class="lang-cpp prettyprint-override"><code>namespace ns {
template &lt;class T&gt;
T foo(int x) {
    A a;
    a.x = x;
    return {};
}
}  // namespace ns
</code></pre>
<p><a href="https://godbolt.org/z/TPMjWfcro" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Demo</a></p>

Q: MFC C++ CButton mouse hover event A: <p>This works for me:</p>
<p>MyDlg.h</p>
<pre><code>public:
    virtual BOOL PreTranslateMessage(MSG* pMsg);
</code></pre>
<p>MyDlg.cpp</p>
<pre><code>BOOL CMyDlg::PreTranslateMessage(MSG* pMsg)
{
    // Pushbutton release
    if (pMsg-&gt;hwnd == GetDlgItem(IDC_MY_PUSHBUTTON)-&gt;m_hWnd &amp;&amp; pMsg-&gt;message == WM_LBUTTONUP)
    {
        // Do Button release stuff;
    }

    return CDialogEx::PreTranslateMessage(pMsg);
}
</code></pre>
